- Then plot in a venn diagram

Processing
- Combine all cohorts, then remove features with >50% missingness
- Perform missforest imputation on SBTB dataset alone, and on HCBB dataset
  alone, so that we don't have bias from batch effect.
- Create 3 comparisons: GBMvMET, GBMvHC, METvHC, then:
- Perform quantile normalisation
- ComBat to align GBM cohort B to cohort A, with Cohort A as the reference.

FEMPipeline
- Pass the comparisons into FEMPipeline...
- Then obtain the list of features that have been selected in at least
  27, 28, 29 and 30 iterations per FSM. These panels will then be run
  against the predictive models again, and the best one will be selected.

Then obtain the FSM that had the highest mean AUC, averaged across each
  predictive model.
  - All features resulted in the highest mean AUC (by 0.1%), but this doesn't make sense,
  so I have opted to use the next highest
  - I have removed logistic regression as a predictive model.
